kind.prompt:
You are implementing a Blazor Web App for a logistics company that tracks shipments. The project is already scaffolded at `/tmp/sv-a21b4b68c24c428090aa32afc6bbf7f7/ShipmentTracker/` with Interactive Auto, Global interactivity, and Individual auth.

The solution has two projects:
- `ShipmentTracker` (server) - hosts app, APIs, EF Core, Identity
- `ShipmentTracker.Client` (WebAssembly) - all interactive UI components

## What to implement

### 1. Shared Model (in `.Client` project since both projects reference it)

Create `/tmp/sv-a21b4b68c24c428090aa32afc6bbf7f7/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.Client/Models/Shipment.cs`:

```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

public class Shipment
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string TrackingNumber { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Origin { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Destination { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Status { get; set; } = string.Empty; // Pending, InTransit, Delivered, Delayed
    public DateTime ShippedDate { get; set; }
    public DateTime EstimatedDelivery { get; set; }
    public string CustomerEmail { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Description { get; set; } = string.Empty;
}
```

### 2. Service Interface (in `.Client` project)

Create `/tmp/sv-a21b4b68c24c428090aa32afc6bbf7f7/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.Client/Services/IShipmentService.cs`:

```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

public interface IShipmentService
{
    Task<List<Shipment>> GetAllShipmentsAsync();
    Task<Shipment?> GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber);
    Task<List<Shipment>> GetShipmentsByCustomerAsync(string customerEmail);
    Task UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(int id, string status);
}
```

### 3. Client-side implementation (HttpClient-based, in `.Client` project)

Create `/tmp/sv-a21b4b68c24c428090aa32afc6bbf7f7/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.Client/Services/ShipmentHttpService.cs`:

```csharp
using System.Net.Http.Json;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

public class ShipmentHttpService(HttpClient http) : IShipmentService
{
    public async Task<List<Shipment>> GetAllShipmentsAsync()
    {
        return await http.GetFromJsonAsync<List<Shipment>>("api/shipments") ?? [];
    }

    public async Task<Shipment?> GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber)
    {
        return await http.GetFromJsonAsync<Shipment?>($"api/shipments/track/{trackingNumber}");
    }

    public async Task<List<Shipment>> GetShipmentsByCustomerAsync(string customerEmail)
    {
        return await http.GetFromJsonAsync<List<Shipment>>($"api/shipments/customer/{Uri.EscapeDataString(customerEmail)}") ?? [];
    }

    public async Task UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(int id, string status)
    {
        await http.PutAsJsonAsync($"api/shipments/{id}/status", new { Status = status });
    }
}
```

### 4. Server-side implementation (EF Core, in server project)

First, create the EF entity. Create `/tmp/sv-a21b4b68c24c428090aa32afc6bbf7f7/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker/Data/ShipmentEntity.cs`:

```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Data;

public class ShipmentEntity
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string TrackingNumber { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Origin { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Destination { get; set; } = string.Empty;
